  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of dizziness and giddiness in the setting of known atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary arteries and nonrheumatic mitral valve insufficiency. Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to evaluate for potential arrhythmias or ischemic changes that may be contributing to these symptomatic episodes. The related diagnosis codes I25.10, I34.0, and R42 support the clinical indication for this diagnostic procedure. Because the required precertification was not obtained before services were rendered, the claim was denied under Reason Code CO-197, and this appeal requests reconsideration of the medical necessity determination."
